        "start_xml_ordinal": 17303,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 668,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 326,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "To ensure convergence the SIP solver uses a relaxation factor. For convergence  should be set lower than one and even then there are certain situations in which the method may fail to converge. Experience has shown that when  the method virtually always converges and this is therefore the default value used in XBeach."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 17404,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 670,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 328,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "The method relies on an iterative solution of the linear system and generates intermediate solutions which improve in accuracy when more iterations are taken. There is usually no need to continue this procedure until machine precision is reached, since the errors made in the underlying discretisation process are usually much larger than the accuracy of the computer arithmetic. A stopping criterion is needed that determines when the solution is considered to be sufficiently accurate. Here, similar as in Stelling and Zijlema (2003), the following criterion is adopted"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 17481,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 672,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 330,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Where is a pre determined threshold,  the right hand side of the linear problem, is the  norm of the respective vector and  the intermediate solution. Interestingly it appears that the solution of the pressure matrix is not very sensitive to the threshold  and it usually suffices to set it to about  (see Stelling and Zijlema, 2002). If for some reason the method has not reached convergence after  iterations the iteration process is also terminated and the last iterative solution is used. By default this is set to iterations."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 17728,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 674,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 332,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Because the SIP solver is based on an incomplete LU factorisation it is an inherently serial algorithm. This makes the SIP solver ill suited for parallelization. Parallelisation through domain decomposition using an explicit coupling between the domains most likely will work, but will require a large number of outer iterations for convergence."
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
  },
